      {
        "id": 221584,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-21T20:33:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm not sure what counts as \"spoilers\" anymore.&nbsp; C&amp;A were holding back on Tactics and RPG info for a while, but not anymore.&nbsp; Some big reveals I can think of which still have some mystery around them:</p><p>Mist Storm:</p><ul>\n<li>Prime War takes place after the \"end\" of the Mist Storm timeline; presumably the Prime Aspects yanked some survivors of their choice out to fight in their games and left the rest to die.&nbsp; We still don't know how the Mist Storm universe manages to be completely destroyed; presumably it's the Mist Storm itself, but we don't really understand what that is or how it works.</li>\n<li>Captain Cosmic somehow defeats Galactra and absorbs her powers.</li>\n</ul><p>Sentinel Comics:</p><ul>\n<li>The Citizens of the Sun have disbanded and are doing their own thing.&nbsp; Notably, Blood, Sweat, and Tears are still hanging out, under new names, and are up to no good, though their intended endgame is still unknown.</li>\n<li>Akash'Flora seems to be some sort of transitional state.&nbsp; It's unknown what it will become afterwards.</li>\n<li>Proletariat is part of a new villain team, Perestroika, along with the new Iron Curtain (the daughter of the original), the Marxman, and an unnamed fourth member.&nbsp; They can be seen on lanyards given out at GenCon.&nbsp; It's been hinted that they'll be in the Sentinels of Freedom video game.</li>\n<li>Captain Cosmic's encounter with Galactra, instead of making him stronger, leaves him weak and stranded on an alien planet.&nbsp; Presumably he'll get rescued at some point, but no one knows he's there.</li>\n<li>Sky-Scraper and K.N.Y.F.E. have new names and a new villain, Malyce (of whom we know nothing).</li>\n<li>Gloomweaver is legitimately free in the universe, but strangely absent from stories so far.&nbsp; Why hasn't he taken over?</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:17.740Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
