      {
        "id": 221591,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-23T20:24:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's not what I meant, actually.&nbsp; In Mist Storm he takes over Medico's body.&nbsp; He's still limited in that form (it's super-powerful, but not full-strength Discordian God powerful) and would prefer to be back in his own body, even if it means returning to the Realm of Discord.&nbsp; But in the RPG timeline, Xian Niu, The Master, breaks him out of the OblivAeon shard and he's just legit free in the world.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wait, wasn't The Master killed by the \"arcane battery\" that he leeched from Nightmist, when she reclaimed that power?&nbsp; How would he be alive to break Gloomweaver out of Medico's shard if he's dead?</p>\n<p>(edit–I stand corrected.&nbsp; The phraseology from the Letters Page was that The Master was \"really messed up\", not dead.&nbsp; Yay research!)</p>",
        "post_number": 10,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:18.198Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 18403,
        "topic_slug": "post-oblivaeon-spoilers-here-only",
        "display_username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"MindWanderer\"]\n\nThat&#39;s not what I meant, actually.&nbsp; In Mist Storm he takes over Medico&#39;s body.&nbsp; He&#39;s still limited in that form (it&#39;s super-powerful, but not full-strength Discordian God powerful) and would prefer to be back in his own body, even if it means returning to the Realm of Discord.&nbsp; But in the RPG timeline, Xian Niu, The Master, breaks him out of the OblivAeon shard and he&#39;s just legit free in the world.\n\n[/quote]\n\nWait, wasn&#39;t The Master killed by the &quot;arcane battery&quot; that he leeched from Nightmist, when she reclaimed that power?&nbsp; How would he be alive to break Gloomweaver out of Medico&#39;s shard if he&#39;s dead?\n\n(edit--I stand corrected.&nbsp; The phraseology from the Letters Page was that The Master was &quot;really messed up&quot;, not dead.&nbsp; Yay research!)\n",
